kstar run
*********

Usage: kstar run [options] <files>...
       kstar <file.kstar>

Runs each program. A folder means every .kstar file inside it, and
`kstar file.kstar` is short for `kstar run file.kstar`. With several files,
each file's output starts with its name, and a count of the files that
passed and failed comes at the end.

Imported files are checked before anything runs. A module's top level runs
the first time one of its names is used, without its print, test, draw and
trace statements.

The exit code is 0 when every program ran without errors and no test
failed, 1 otherwise, and 2 when the command itself was wrong.

Options:
  --out <dir>         where `draw` writes its files (default: the current
                      folder)
  --allow-path <dir>  let std.io also read and write files in <dir>; give it
                      more than once for more folders. Without it a program may
                      only use files in its own folder.
  --fixed-clock       std.benchmark reports every time as 0, so the output is
                      the same on every run
  --watch             run again whenever a file changes; stop with Ctrl-C
  --trace-calls       print every function call with its arguments, and every
                      return with its result
  --eager-imports     run each imported module at its import line, not when one
                      of its names is first used
  --theme <name>      the colours of drawings and of the page `draw M on "w"`
                      writes: auto (the default: the page follows the system,
                      drawings are light), light, dark or high-contrast. Without
                      it, the KSTAR_THEME environment variable or `theme =
                      "<name>"` in the config file (~/.config/kstar/config.toml,
                      or %APPDATA%\kstar\config.toml on Windows) decides.
  --color <when>      auto (the default), always or never. With auto, output is
                      coloured only on a terminal and never when the NO_COLOR
                      environment variable is set.

Examples:
  kstar run examples/tour.kstar
      run one program
  kstar run labs/ --out drawings
      run every program in labs/, writing drawings into drawings/
  kstar run --theme dark lab1.kstar
      run lab1.kstar, drawing in the dark theme


