kstar fmt
*********

Usage: kstar fmt [--check] <files>...
       kstar fmt -

Rewrites each file in the standard style. A folder means every .kstar file
inside it, and `-` reads a program from standard input and writes the
formatted program to standard output, for editors and scripts.

Options:
  --check             change nothing; list the files that need formatting and
                      exit with code 1 if there are any

Examples:
  kstar fmt lab1.kstar
      format one file in place
  kstar fmt --check .
      list the files in this folder that are not formatted
  kstar fmt - < lab1.kstar
      print lab1.kstar formatted, changing nothing


