kstar repl
**********

Usage: kstar repl [options]

An interactive prompt: type statements or expressions and see the results.
A bare expression is printed, and names can be defined again. Inside it,
`:type <expr>` shows a type, `:trace M <word>` traces a machine,
`:load <file>` runs a file, `:reset` forgets everything, and `:help` and
`:quit` do what they say. Tab completes names.

Options:
  --trace-calls       print every function call with its arguments, and every
                      return with its result
  --theme <name>      the colours of drawings and of the page `draw M on "w"`
                      writes: auto (the default: the page follows the system,
                      drawings are light), light, dark or high-contrast. Without
                      it, the KSTAR_THEME environment variable or `theme =
                      "<name>"` in the config file (~/.config/kstar/config.toml,
                      or %APPDATA%\kstar\config.toml on Windows) decides.
  --color <when>      auto (the default), always or never. With auto, output is
                      coloured only on a terminal and never when the NO_COLOR
                      environment variable is set.

Examples:
  kstar repl
      start the prompt
  kstar repl --trace-calls
      start it, showing every call


