kstar trace
***********

Usage: kstar trace [options] <file> <machine> <word>

Runs the file without showing its output, then shows every step of
<machine> on <word>, as `trace <machine> on "<word>"` would at the end of
the file. <machine> may be any expression, such as `to_dfa(r)`. Use "" for
the empty word.

Options:
  --color <when>      auto (the default), always or never. With auto, output is
                      coloured only on a terminal and never when the NO_COLOR
                      environment variable is set.

Examples:
  kstar trace examples/01_dfa.kstar HasDouble1 0110
      trace a DFA on 0110
  kstar trace lab.kstar "to_dfa(r)" ""
      trace an expression on the empty word


